Description: pvr: copy deferred control streams of any size
 vkCmdExecuteCommands() copies the host-side control stream of a secondary
 command buffer recorded with RENDER_PASS_CONTINUE and SIMULTANEOUS_USE into
 the primary with pvr_arch_csb_copy() (pvr_arch_csb.c). The function passed
 the stream size in bytes to pvr_arch_csb_alloc_dwords(), which takes dwords,
 so four times the needed space was reserved, and a stream larger than one
 control stream buffer only reached pvr_finishme() and an assert.
 pvr_csb_buffer_extend() always allocated one PVR_CMD_BUFFER_CSB_BO_SIZE
 buffer and did not check that the request fits into it. With assertions
 disabled, from about 1000 bytes of secondary control stream the reservation
 ended beyond the buffer object, and the copy or the next commands of the
 primary, including the stream link, were written past its end.
 .
 pvr_csb_buffer_extend() now takes the requested size and allocates a buffer
 that holds the relocated state update, the request and the reserved link and
 guard space, rounded up to PVR_CMD_BUFFER_CSB_BO_SIZE. Buffers of the
 standard size are still taken from and returned to the per-device pool;
 pvr_csb_bo_release() frees larger ones instead of pooling them.
 pvr_arch_csb_copy() passes the size in dwords and sets the relocation mark,
 so a link to a new buffer is placed at the current end of the destination
 and the copied stream stays contiguous.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
